* MC3340 electronic attenuator (Motorola), transistor level.
* Topology and resistor values: Motorola's internal schematic, as transcribed
* in MAME's netlist library (src/lib/netlist/macro/nlm_opamp_lib.cpp,
* MC3340_DIP, licence CC0-1.0, by Colin Howell), which restores the
* cross-connection missing from the 1990s data books and the two diodes of
* the 1979 data book. Transistor and diode models are that netlist's
* (generic NPN, IS raised to match Motorola's attenuation curve).
* This is a component model, not Monaco GP circuitry.
* Pins: 1 IN, 2 CONTROL, 3 GND, 6 ROLLOFF, 7 OUTPUT, 8 VCC
.subckt MC3340 in ctl gnd roll out vcc
.model QMC NPN(IS=1e-13 BF=100)
.model DMC D(IS=1e-15 N=1)
R1  vcc n1 5.1k
D1  n1 n1k DMC
R2  n1k gnd 4.7k
Q1  vcc n1 e1 QMC
R3  e1 b2 750
R4  b2 gnd 10k
Q2  vcc b2 e2 QMC
R5  e1 b3 750
R6  b3 ctli 3.9k
* Control offset (3 November 2026): the transistor model reaches each
* attenuation about 0.13 V of CONTROL earlier than Motorola's typical 12 V
* curve (data sheet Figure 3, "Attenuation versus DC Control Voltage";
* 0.10-0.20 V from 2 to 34 dB). This source moves the whole curve onto it.
VCOFS ctl ctli DC 0.13
Q3  vcc b3 e3 QMC
R7  vcc n7 5.1k
R8  in n7 20k
D2  n7 n7k DMC
R9  n7k gnd 510
Q4  vcc e3 e46 QMC
Q5  e46 in e5 QMC
R10 e5 gnd 1.3k
Q6  roll e2 e46 QMC
Q7  vcc e2 e79 QMC
Q8  e79 b8 e8 QMC
R12 e8 gnd 1.5k
Q9  roll e3 e79 QMC
R11 e2 gnd 5.1k
R14 e3 gnd 5.1k
R13 vcc roll 6.2k
Q10 vcc roll out_e QMC
R15 out_e gnd 5.1k
R16 out_e out 200
R17 vcc b8 5.1k
D3  b8 b8k DMC
R18 b8k gnd 510
.ends MC3340
